# double_free_scan's per-slot state bytes (heap/slotstate.rs): a byte
# array outside every verified invariant. Verus checks the indexing and
# the arithmetic (the addresses wrap); the verified wrappers (free, claim,
# pop, release, the batch loops, check_not_cached) only turn what `step`
# returns into aborts (`abort_pending`); none changes what the verified
# paths do. `commit`'s range lying in `init`'s reservation is not
# verified either (`mprotect` is specified only for its call).

# The arrays' initialiser: an array repeat of an element that is not
# `Copy`, which Verus does not take. It claims nothing, and it is
# evaluated at compile time.
NO_ARRAYS	core library	none (assumption)

# The byte at an address `byte` computes: a slot index below the
# watermark that `commit` precedes, in an array `init` reserved. That
# protocol is not a verified fact; it claims nothing about the byte.
byte_at	raw pointer (internal)	RefinedRust

# The double-free window's premise (theorem_double_free_window): a
# permission to the byte `step` operates on, whose value is a state, the
# one the last step on that slot left. No verified invariant ties the
# bytes to the caches or the bitmap (#397); the operations are
# vspec::byte's wrappers; the free's race is tests/loom/src/slotstate.rs.
# Called only in step (tests::slot_byte_axiom_is_called_only_in_step).
axiom_slot_byte	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
